6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-11-11 (PST): reproduced RED on git 2.56 (150 loose objects plus a planted 13 h-old lock: `run_auto_maintenance` rc 0, nothing packed). Chose option (a): before each explicit step, reclaim a lock older than 12 h (git's gc.pid rule) using the shared revalidating `git_locking._reclaim_if_stale`, extracted from the index.lock reclaim, and log a warning. The lock literal is marker-admitted against the new sunset ticket `sulfuric-zebraic-hackee`, not this bug. The commit is stacked on the axisdeer change because both edit the same ADR 0051 and concurrency.md sentences (worktree fix-git-kill-lock). Tests: the stale lock is reclaimed and the objects are packed; a young lock is left alone and nothing is packed.","timestamp":1794445567616990157},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 (PST): CLOSED (class preexisting) through the completion gate. Fix merged as Gerrit 3357 at `614175831f6`, stacked on 3356. Before each explicit maintenance step, `run_auto_maintenance` removes a `<common-dir>/objects/maintenance.lock` older than 12 h (git's own gc.pid staleness rule) using the shared revalidating `git_locking._reclaim_if_stale`, and logs a warning when it does. The lock literal's mechanism marker names the sunset task `sulfuric-zebraic-hackee` (open, P4): retire the reclaim once git expires the lock itself or maintenance moves out of the write path. Production: the next write after deploy self-heals any stale lock older than 12 h. No operator action is needed.","timestamp":1794456984596947731}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794427120762890197,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"57d8b3ef-eaf3-4911-af50-dd82ee023fd2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"51e0-5038-bf00-4653"},{"link_uuid":"206d179a-5e9f-4717-90b4-ed15860d119b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5b5d-216c-d207-41e7"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nrebar's explicit post-write maintenance step (`event_commit_git.run_auto_maintenance`) runs `git maintenance run --auto ...` under the store write lock. Git takes `objects/maintenance.lock` before it evaluates any task, and holds it for the whole run. If the process is SIGKILLed while it holds the lock, the lock file stays behind. That can happen when a container is replaced or OOM-killed. Git never expires this lock, and `maintenance run --auto` then exits 0 without doing any work. Store maintenance therefore stops permanently, with no signal.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production clone `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`: a lock dated 2026-09-03 01:36:18 UTC stopped all maintenance until 2026-11-11 (bug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek`).\n- Reproduced on git 2.47.3 inside the MCP container and on git 2.56 locally: with the lock file present, `git maintenance run --auto` and `git maintenance run --task=...` exit 0, print nothing, and do nothing. Re-checked 2026-11-11 on git 2.56: 122 loose objects, lock planted, `--auto --task=loose-objects` rc 0 and nothing packed; lock removed, same command packed all 122.\n- Upstream `builtin/gc.c` `maintenance_run_tasks`: on failing `repo_hold_lock_file_for_update(.../maintenance)` it warns only without `--auto`/quiet and returns 0. There is no staleness check. By contrast git's own `gc.pid` lock (`lock_repo_for_gc`) is treated as stale once older than `12 * 3600` seconds.\n\n## What the parent fix already covers\n\nBug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek`: bounded git children no longer start implicit maintenance; the explicit step runs only incremental tasks (0.35-17.3 s on the 1.07M-object store); a timed-out step is reaped as a process group with SIGTERM, so git deletes its own lock. One window remains: a hard kill during the explicit step itself.\n\n## Decision: reclaim a stale lock under the write lock (option a)\n\n- (a) chosen: before each explicit step, while holding rebar's write lock, remove `<common-dir>/objects/maintenance.lock` when its mtime is older than 12 hours, then run maintenance as usual. Self-healing with no operator action, and it runs on every store (local and production) at the point maintenance is attempted.\n- (b) rejected: clearing at container start is unsafe because 2 MCP containers can share one tickets clone during an autodeploy overlap, so \"the old container is gone\" is not guaranteed; it also never runs for local stores.\n- (c) rejected: report-only leaves maintenance disabled until a human acts.\n\nWhy 12 hours: the lock's mtime is its creation time (git does not refresh it). The longest legitimate holder seen is a full gc at 605.6 s on the production store; rebar's own step is bounded at 120 s plus a 5 s grace. 12 hours is git's own staleness rule for `gc.pid`, well beyond any real run, and still bounds the outage to half a day instead of forever. rebar's write lock does not cover a non-rebar git run in another worktree sharing the object DB, so the age bound (not the write lock) is what proves staleness. The removal revalidates device and inode first, as the index.lock reclaim does, so a lock replaced in the window survives. A reclaim logs a warning naming the path and age.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py`: extract the stat/revalidate/remove body of `_reclaim_if_stale_index_lock` into `_reclaim_if_stale(lock_file, *, stale_s, force)`; the index-lock function calls it (behavior unchanged).\n2. `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`: `run_auto_maintenance` resolves the common git dir (`_resolve_common_git_dir`, pure filesystem), calls `_reclaim_if_stale` on `objects/maintenance.lock` with a 12 h bound, logs when it removed one, then runs git as before. The new `maintenance.lock` literal carries a `# mechanism-ok: lock maintenance.lock` marker whose reason cites ADR 0051 (it is git's lock, not a new rebar lock).\n3. `tests/unit/test_store_maintenance_lock_reclaim.py` (new): real git repo with >100 loose objects; a 13 h-old planted lock is reclaimed and the loose objects get packed; a fresh lock is left in place and nothing is packed.\n4. `docs/concurrency.md` scale-up paragraph and ADR 0051 amendment: one sentence each.\n\nNo config key, env var, or flag.\n\n## Resolution\n\nLanded as Gerrit 3357, merged `614175831f6`, stacked on 3356 (`idle-ammoniacal-axisdeer`) because both edit the same ADR and concurrency.md sentences. The ratchet now requires a marker to open with a sunset ticket, so the `lock maintenance.lock` marker names the new sunset task `sulfuric-zebraic-hackee` (retire the reclaim once git expires the lock itself), not this bug. The stale-lock test fails on the pre-fix code: nothing is packed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A stranded `objects/maintenance.lock` cannot stop store maintenance permanently, or its presence is reported through a surface an operator reads.\n- [x] A test plants a stale lock and shows that maintenance resumes or that the condition is reported.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `make verify` passes on the change.\n  provenance: environment=local macOS worktree at the stacked change tip, rebar 0.15.1 venv, git 2.56; principal=Rebar Bot Nava, session rebar-session-3d705fec; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — make verify exited 0 (default tier 21084 passed, integration tier 218 passed) and CI cast Verified +1 on the Gerrit change","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5b5d-216c-d207-41e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5ace0e86-51f7-40a3-9096-17c52bfefd74","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3e48-86e5-45a7-4acd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A hard kill during the store's explicit maintenance step strands objects/maintenance.lock and silently stops maintenance","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c2fa5b5d-a293-4ea5-9bb9-cd0d8978fdde","46d4b84e-27db-4df2-a9ec-7deefe567bed","991176d6-fc70-443f-b86c-5443fb49b158","114b4b9b-69c5-4d6e-9785-6b2d44f28187","8874f010-a06a-4a1c-b774-304d09de0e5a","206d179a-5e9f-4717-90b4-ed15860d119b","0bd16528-344d-4a7a-8d51-dd3e54c4e2b2","25e521d5-2d8c-42a9-abf9-73be3184d0b3","5ace0e86-51f7-40a3-9096-17c52bfefd74","9d7108c4-c067-4f5c-84b8-be85c814e2ad","c4db3e5c-0ab7-4d18-b96c-7b02e213903c"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794456984596947732,"uuid":"f1725e54-5214-4a61-9e71-31f5f4e461f6"}